# Cursor Rules — Language

## Requirement

All Cursor rules (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`) must be written in **English**.

## Scope

- **Rule content** — sections, explanations, examples
- **Frontmatter** — `description` field
- **Code comments** inside rule examples (when they illustrate the rule itself)

## Why

- Rules are shared across teams and tools; English is the common technical language
- AI tooling and rule pickers work better with consistent language
- Easier to integrate with external docs and open-source conventions

## When Creating or Editing Rules

1. Write all new rules in English
2. When updating existing rules, keep or convert content to English
3. Exception: examples that demonstrate localized UI (e.g. Russian strings in app code) — the rule text stays in English; the example can show the actual localized value
